  "details": "Players without FBT should be able to enter a \"fake FBT\" mode where they can pose their hips and feet by moving around \"virtual trackers\" to choose a comfortable sitting pose for a situation.   Having to use only the animations that are baked into their avatar, or whatever animation is baked into a seat, is limiting, even though half the time the point of FBT is just to sit naturally somewhere while still mostly only moving your head and hands...    Being able to choose positions right in VR for your non-tracked limbs would help non-FBT players stick out less.",
